  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "For any $\\triangle ABC$, prove that\n$$\\sin A+\\sin B+\\sin C=4\\cos\\frac A2\\cdot\\cos\\frac B2\\cdot\\cos\\frac C2.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sin A+\\sin B+\\sin C=4\\cos\\frac A2\\cos\\frac B2\\cos\\frac C2$.\n\nUse $A+B+C=\\pi$, the sum-to-product formulas and $\\sin C=2\\sin\\frac C2\\cos\\frac C2$.",
      "worked": "Since $A+B+C=\\pi$, we have $A+B=\\pi-C$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\sin A+\\sin B+\\sin C&=2\\sin\\frac{A+B}{2}\\cos\\frac{A-B}{2}+2\\sin\\frac C2\\cos\\frac C2\\\\\n\\sin A+\\sin B+\\sin C&=2\\cos\\frac C2\\cos\\frac{A-B}{2}+2\\sin\\frac C2\\cos\\frac C2\\\\\n\\sin A+\\sin B+\\sin C&=2\\cos\\frac C2\\left(\\cos\\frac{A-B}{2}+\\sin\\frac C2\\right)\\\\\n\\sin A+\\sin B+\\sin C&=2\\cos\\frac C2\\left(\\cos\\frac{A-B}{2}+\\cos\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right)\\\\\n\\sin A+\\sin B+\\sin C&=4\\cos\\frac C2\\cos\\frac A2\\cos\\left(-\\frac B2\\right)\\\\\n\\sin A+\\sin B+\\sin C&=4\\cos\\frac A2\\cos\\frac B2\\cos\\frac C2.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 75
  },
